--boundary-t2
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="UTF-8"

I'm working on the SSE (Server-Sent Events) implementation for
real-time mail notifications. Need to decide on event format.

Option A (simple):
  event: new-mail
  data: {"folder":"inbox","count":3}

Option B (HTMX-native):
  event: new-mail
  data: <div id="inbox-badge" hx-swap-oob="true">3</div>

Option C (hybrid):
  event: new-mail
  data: {"folder":"inbox","count":3,"html":"<div...>"}

I'm leaning toward B since we're all-in on HTMX. The server can
render the partial HTML and the client just swaps it in. No JS
needed to update the UI.

Downside: if we ever want a non-HTMX client (mobile app, CLI),
option B is useless. But that's a bridge we can cross later.

- Bob

